Agent discovery now looks in subfolders, so an agent file at .claude/agents/review/reviewer.md is found, the same way Claude Code finds it. All checks pass: fmt, clippy with -D warnings, and the full cargo test run (7225 passed in the main suite, 19/19 in the agent-discovery tests). The work is committed as 6351c755.

What changed (src/agent_defs.rs, via a new walk_agent_dir):
• Scope: all four agents directories (.yoyo/agents and .claude/agents, in the project and under ~) are searched recursively. A nested file gets the same scope as a top-level one.
• Depth limit: at most 8 levels of subfolders. A deeper folder is listed under Skipped: with the reason.
• Symlinks: a symlinked folder is not followed and is listed under Skipped:. The agents directory itself can still be a symlink, and a symlinked .md file is still read, because the existing file check already follows links. That decision is written in a comment.
• Order: entries are visited in sorted path order. Before this change, two files in one directory with the same name went to whichever came first alphabetically, and the other was shown as shadowed. Nested files follow that same rule. The rules between directories are unchanged.
• Text: the listing header now reads subfolders up to 8 levels deep, with the 8 taken from the depth constant. I removed every "not recursive" claim from src/ and updated docs/src/usage/commands.md and the ARCHITECTURE.md entry, which marks the old claim as superseded.

Tests:
• One existing test checked that a nested file was not loaded. I inverted it: that file is now found, with project scope. The commit message says so.
• Four new tests cover:
  • a file in a subfolder
  • 8 levels deep found, 9 levels deep skipped
  • symlinked folders skipped (including a link that loops back to the agents directory) while a symlinked file still loads
  • which file wins when two subfolders hold the same name
• As a check on the symlink test, I switched the symlink check off and the symlink test failed by name. With the check restored, all 19 pass. With the check off, the looping link still stopped at the depth limit.

Live run: yoyo agents on a temporary repo found review/reviewer.md and listed both the 9-deep folder and the symlinked folder as skipped. The output is pasted in the commit message.

I commented on #1250 with what landed, the depth limit and the symlink rule. The comment also points out one stale line I didn't touch because it's outside this task: the first line of yoyo agents still says "preview: … not yet used by yoyo", which has been false since the agent tool landed in Task 1.
